{
  "description": "Shared OpenBridge icon mapping (NauticPi and NauticPinnace). One entry per icon; a generator per project turns it into its own format (SVG sprite, bitmap font).",
  "source": {
    "title": "OpenBridge Icon Pack",
    "author": "OpenBridge",
    "figmaFileId": "1445713209741917748",
    "url": "https://www.figma.com/community/file/1445713209741917748/openbridge-icon-pack",
    "exportDate": "2026-09-29",
    "exportedWith": "Figma plugin API exportAsync, format SVG_STRING, from a draft duplicate of the Community file",
    "licence": "CC BY 4.0",
    "licenceUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
    "export": "Provenance/OpenBridge/openbridge-figma-export.json in the workspace folder that holds the repositories (next to them, never inside one). Do not publish it: it also holds the OpenBridge and OICL logos. Its provenance note and a dated screenshot of the licence badge lie beside it.",
    "exportSha256": "a4e1b843c8006e7e37edb4f94294e27bee5c36526d5992375a044bb9fe1fdc2e"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Icons ending in -google are based on Google Material Icons (Google LLC, Apache-2.0).",
    "Icons ending in -iec are OpenBridge redrawings of IEC 62288 symbols; no IEC rights are granted.",
    "Never take icons from the OpenBridge GitHub repository (AGPL) or from npm releases for this map; the geometry here is the Figma export under CC BY 4.0.",
    "Do not use the logo-openbridge or logo-oicl components."
  ],
  "fields": {
    "id": "Stable icon name, the OpenBridge repository file name (Figma name lower-cased, spaces removed, aa/ae/oe for the Norwegian letters, % dropped). NauticPi uses it as the sprite id ob-<id>.",
    "figma": "The Figma component name.",
    "node": "Figma node id, set where the name alone is ambiguous or differs from id; otherwise null.",
    "concepts": "What the icon stands for (from the icon evaluation); the first candidate per concept is the primary choice there.",
    "mono": "Optional. How a multi-colour icon becomes single-colour: \"holes\" (white shapes are cut out of the shape below, a stroke outline that only repeats the edge is dropped), \"drop-light\" (light colour layers are dropped, the dark outline stays), \"flatten\" (every layer becomes the one colour). Without it: every colour becomes the one colour, light greys become 35 % of it."
  },
  "resolve": "node id first, then the exact Figma name, then the sanitised name (see id), then the name of the enclosing Figma frame (ignoring frames called outlined/filled). A name that matches more than one component is an error, never a silent pick.",
